newJitLoopT -- SEQ 526 (S4 of docs/jitterWalkRecon.md): the loops, break, continue, return through the walk. Plain = the twin; pop.sh inserts jitter; after the last
lpNew. l1 / l2 / l3 / l4 while, break (WH-3 / WH-7), continue, nested (WH-6). l5..l8 do: twice, once on a false test, break, continue reaching the test.
l9 / la return in a loop, bare and computed. lb / lc a handed-over if carrying a break and a continue: the run-time signal lands on the compiled loop.
ld / le a break in a braced arm (TL-10): the arm's seq catches it, the statement after runs. lf a number crossing a condition. lg / lh conditions that
hand the loop over (a string, a bare read). li a body that never runs, its local read after (the written mark). lj a for, handed over, its break inside.
lk a break at the action's seq: the action ends. ll a statement after a continue is reachable to the walk, never to the run. lm a seq arm in a loop is the
loop's bodySeq, so its break leaves the loop. ln a handed-over if's break landing on the compiled seq arm around it, so the statement after that arm runs.
